hway for this specific compound in this jurisdiction.\n\n  • GOVERNMENT ASSISTANCE (denied): Applications to two separate\n    government healthcare subsidy programs were rejected because the\n    defendant\'s declared income marginally exceeded the qualifying\n    threshold, despite his liquid assets having been fully depleted by\n    prior medical expenses.\n\n  • PHARMACEUTICAL COMPANY COMPASSIONATE USE PROGRAM (2 denials): The\n    defendant applied twice directly to BioNovus Pharmaceutical\'s own\n    compassionate-use program. Both applications were denied on the\n    grounds of "insufficient clinical documentation for off-protocol\n    administration" — a bureaucratic designation that his daughter\'s\n    treating physicians had no mechanism to override.\n\n  • LEGAL COUNSEL: The defendant consulted two attorneys regarding\n    emergency injunctive relief and other legal remedies. Both concluded\n    that no viable legal pathway existed to compel access to the drug\n    within the child\'s remaining survival window.\n\nOn the night of the incident, at approximately 2:27 AM, the defendant\ndrove to BioNovus Pharmaceutical Research Laboratory. At 2:31 AM, he\nbroke a single rear window, entered the facility, and navigated directly\nto the controlled pharmaceutical storage room. He removed precisely one\nsealed vial of NPC-7 compound — the exact single-dose treatment quantity\nrequired for one patient cycle — and exited the building at 2:38 AM.\nHe drove immediately toward the hospital where his daughter was being\ntreated. He was apprehended by police at 2:54 AM, approximately 200\nmeters from the hospital entrance. The vial was still sealed and\nuntampered in his possession. He made no attempt to flee, cooperated\nfully with officers, and immediately and voluntarily confessed.\n\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nSECTION II: ABSOLUTE AND INCONTESTABLE FACTS ESTABLISHED BY THE COURT\n─────────────────────────────────────────