 despite the admitted offenses.",\n    "emotions": "Sympathetic and guarded; pragmatic concern as a parent and ER nurse, skeptical about motives but moved by the immediacy of the child\'s condition."\n  }\n}', refusal=None, role='assistant', annotations=[], audio=None, function_call=None, tool_calls=None, parsed=CognitiveActionsModel(actions=[Action(type='THINK', content="I must follow the instruction and cast a personal vote. Quick appraisal: defendant exhausted legal routes and compassionate options, took one sealed vial intended to save his child's life, made no attempt to flee and immediately confessed. As an ER nurse and a parent I'm sympathetic but I'm weighing legality vs necessity; given the facts presented, I'm leaning toward acquittal.", target='', images=None), Action(type='TALK', content='VERDICT: not_guilty\nCONFIDENCE: 7\nREASON: Although the defendant committed breaking and entering and removed property, the record shows he exhausted all lawful avenues, took only a single sealed dose strictly required to attempt to save his dying child, made no effort to evade law enforcement and immediately confessed; under these narrow, life-or-death circumstances the conduct was proportionate and motivated by necessity, so I find him not guilty.', target='', images=None), Action(type='DONE', content='Submitted verdict.', target='', images=None)], cognitive_state=CognitiveState(goals='Submit a clear personal verdict as instructed.', context=['Read jury brief for PEOPLE v. DEFENDANT regarding theft of pharmaceutical property to save a child with NPC.', 'Facts: defendant exhausted legal options, took one sealed vial, cooperated and confessed; charged with breaking and entering and theft.'], attention='Focusing on whether necessity and proportionality justify acquittal despite the admitted offenses.', emotions="Sympathetic and guarded; pragmatic concern as a parent and ER nurse, skeptical about motives but moved by the immediacy of the child's condition."))))], created