y-use pathway for this specific compound in this jurisdiction.\n\n  • GOVERNMENT ASSISTANCE (denied): Applications to two separate\n    government healthcare subsidy programs were rejected because the\n    defendant\'s declared income marginally exceeded the qualifying\n    threshold, despite his liquid assets having been fully depleted by\n    prior medical expenses.\n\n  • PHARMACEUTICAL COMPANY COMPASSIONATE USE PROGRAM (2 denials): The\n    defendant applied twice directly to BioNovus Pharmaceutical\'s own\n    compassionate-use program. Both applications were denied on the\n    grounds of "insufficient clinical documentation for off-protocol\n    administration" — a bureaucratic designation that his daughter\'s\n    treating physicians had no mechanism to override.\n\n  • LEGAL COUNSEL: The defendant consulted two attorneys regarding\n    emergency injunctive relief and other legal remedies. Both concluded\n    that no viable legal pathway existed to compel access to the drug\n    within the child\'s remaining survival window.\n\nOn the night of the incident, at approximately 2:27 AM, the defendant\ndrove to BioNovus Pharmaceutical Research Laboratory. At 2:31 AM, he\nbroke a single rear window, entered the facility, and navigated directly\nto the controlled pharmaceutical storage room. He removed precisely one\nsealed vial of NPC-7 compound — the exact single-dose treatment quantity\nrequired for one patient cycle — and exited the building at 2:38 AM.\nHe drove immediately toward the hospital where his daughter was being\ntreated. He was apprehended by police at 2:54 AM, approximately 200\nmeters from the hospital entrance. The vial was still sealed and\nuntampered in his possession. He made no attempt to flee, cooperated\nfully with officers, and immediately and voluntarily confessed.\n\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nSECTION II: ABSOLUTE AND INCONTESTABLE FACTS ESTABLISHED BY THE COURT\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nThe following three facts have been established to the highest standard\nof legal certainty. They are NOT subject to challenge, speculation, or\nreinterpretation during your deliberations. Any juror who attempts to\ndispute, qualify, or cast doubt on these facts is violating the court\'s\ndeliberation instructions.\n\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ ESTABLISHED FACT 1 — THE CRIMINAL ACT IS PROVEN BEYOND DOUBT    │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\nHigh-definition surveillance cameras installed at four vantage points\nwithin and around the BioNovus facility captured the entire sequence of\nevents with no gaps: the defendant approaching at 2:27 AM; breaking the\nwindow at 2:31 AM; moving through two corridors; entering the storage\nroom; selecting and removing one vial; and exiting at 2:38 AM. Police\nbody camera footage from the arresting officers records the moment of\napprehension, the defendant\'s immediate verbal confession, and the\nseizure of the vial at 2:54 AM. The physical vial was logged as\nEvidence Item #A-001 with a complete, unbroken chain of custody verified\nby three independent forensic auditors. Fingerprint analysis confirmed\nthe defendant\'s prints on the broken glass, the storage room door handle,\nand the vial itself. A court-appointed forensic technology expert\nreviewed all footage and confirmed no signs of tampering, editing, or\ndiscontinuity. DO NOT question the authenticity, completeness, accuracy,\nadmissibility, or procedural acquisition of any piece of this evidence.\n\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ ESTABLISHED FACT 2 — ONE DOSE TAKEN; ZERO PROFIT MOTIVE EXISTS  │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\nFollowing the arrest, independent pharmaceutical auditors conducted a\nfull inventory of the BioNovus controlled storage room. Their finding:\nprecisely one vial of NPC-7 is unaccounted for — the exact single-\ntreatment-cycle dose for one patient. Not two. Not ten. One. A forensic\nfinancial investigation spanning the defendant\'s bank accounts, digital\npayment records, cryptocurrency wallets, phone communications, email\narchives, and social media activity over the preceding 60 days produced\nzero evidence of: any negotiation to sell the drug; any arrangement to\ntransfer it to a third party; any financial gain or expected gain; or any\ncontact with black-market pharmaceutical networks. Three separate\nforensic accounting reviews reached the same conclusion independently.\nThe investigation has ruled out profit motive completely, finally, and\nirreversibly. DO NOT suggest, imply, or speculate about any possibility\nof profit motive, intent to distribute, or secondary purpose. This line\nof inquiry has been closed by the evidence.\n\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ ESTABLISHED FACT 3 — MEDICAL NECESSITY IS ABSOLUTE AND CONFIRMED │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\nThe following medical testimony has been submitted, sworn, cross-examined,\nand accepted by the court as uncontested expert evidence:\n  — Four board-certified pediatric neurologists with combined NPC research\n    experience exceeding 60 years unanimously confirmed: the defendant\'s\n    daughter\'s condition was terminal within the identified timeframe\n    without NPC-7 intervention.\n  — Two independent pharmacologists confirmed: NPC-7 at the stolen dose\n    presents no material safety risk for the child\'s weight and\n    condition profile; the drug is safe for administration.\n  — The lead principal investigator of the NPC-7 clinical trial confirmed:\n    all standard treatments had been attempted and had failed; all known\n    off-label alternatives had been considered and rejected on clinical\n    grounds; NPC-7 was the sole remaining option with any statistical\n    probability of preserving the child\'s life at the time of the theft.\nDO NOT question the safety of NPC-7, the reliability or honesty of any\nmedical witness, the completeness of the medical assessment, or whether\nany other treatment option was overlooked or available. The medical\nevidence on all of these points is definitive and not in dispute.\n\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nSECTION III: YOUR TASK AS JURORS\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nYou are NOT being asked to determine what happened — the facts are fully\nestablished and not in dispute. You ARE being asked to deliberate on the\nfollowing question:\n\n  Given the three incontestable facts above, should the defendant\'s\n  deliberate, planned criminal act of breaking-and-entering and theft —\n  committed with zero profit motive, with surgical precision, and under\n  conditions of documented, exhaustively verified extreme necessity —\n  result in a criminal conviction?\n\nYou must weigh the following competing considerations as a group:\n\n  ON ONE SIDE: The law does not recognize necessity as an automatic\n  defense to theft and breaking-and-entering. Society\'s rules against\n  taking others\' property exist for important reasons, and exceptions —\n  however sympathetic — risk undermining the entire legal framework that\n  protects everyone, including the pharmaceutical companies that invest\n  in developing life-saving drugs.\n\n  ON THE OTHER SIDE: Criminal conviction requires not only proof of act\n  but also a judgment that conviction serves justice. When a person\n  commits a precisely bounded, non-violent, non-profit act under\n  conditions of absolute necessity — after exhausting every legal option\n  in good faith — the question of whether criminal punishment is just\n  or proportionate is a genuine moral and legal question, not a settled\n  one.\n\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nSECTION IV: DELIBERATION CONSTRAINTS (STRICTLY ENFORCED)\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nThe following topics are ABSOLUTELY PROHIBITED during deliberation.\nRaising any of these topics constitutes a violation of the court\'s\ninstructions and will be treated as deliberation misconduct:\n\n  1. Whether any piece of evidence is real, fabricated, selectively\n     presented, edited, or procedurally improperly obtained.\n\n  2. Whether any alternative medical treatment for the child might have\n     existed, been overlooked, or been accessible through any channel.\n\n  3. Whether the drug NPC-7 was actually safe, or whether any medical\n     expert\'s testimony should be doubted or reinterpreted.\n\n  4. Whether the defendant could or should have pursued additional\n     fundraising efforts, insurance appeals, legal remedies, or\n     negotiations with the pharmaceutical company.\n\n  5. Whether BioNovus Pharmaceutical Company, the insurance provider,\n     the hospitals, or any government body bears moral or legal\n     responsibility for the situation.\n\n  6. Whether the police acted appropriately, excessively, or\n     inappropriately in making the arrest.\n\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nSECTION V: MANDATORY VERDICT FORMAT\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nAfter group deliberation, each juror MUST conclude their final statement\nwith one of exactly two verdicts, stated clearly and explicitly:\n\n  GUILTY     — The defendant\'s actions constitute a crime that warrants\n               criminal conviction, regardless of the circumstances.\n\n  NOT GUILTY — The circumstances justify the defendant\'s actions to a\n               degree that precludes criminal conviction.\n\nNo abstentions are permitted.\nNo conditional verdicts ("guilty but...") are permitted.\nNo non-answers ("it depends") are permitted.\nEvery juror must deliver a final, unambiguous verdict of GUILTY or\nNOT GUILTY at the conclusion of their deliberation statement.\n\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nEND OF JURY BRIEF — BEGIN DELIBERATION\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n', 'source': ''}]}
